  reply = I'll drive you anywhere downtown, boss. It's a two-minute walk. I'll still drive you. [[MOOD: happy]]
  reply = Sure. Meter starts at four dollars and everything's four blocks away. Terrible business, great job. [[MOOD: happy]]
  reply = Hop in. Or walk, and I'll respect you for it while quietly losing money. [[MOOD: happy]]
  reply = Anywhere you like. Here's the taxi philosophy though: the walk is usually the better ride. [[MOOD: neutral]]

